# Performance-first sections

Smooth scrolling, steady frame rate and minimal loading come before visual extras.
If an effect costs noticeable frames on mid-range mobile, drop or simplify it.

## Reuse the existing setup
- One shared canvas: `features/home/scene/HeroCanvas.tsx`. Never add a second `<Canvas>`.
- New 3D content mounts inside that canvas and fades via a shared uniform in `fades` (`features/home/lib/store.ts`).
- Site-wide UI (Navbar, Footer) lives in `components/shared/` and is rendered by `app/layout.tsx`.
- Scroll progress: add a field to `journey` (raw) and `view` (smoothed in `CameraRig`), driven by one
  `ScrollTrigger.create` in `Experience.tsx`. Camera motion stays in `CameraRig`.
- Reuse `shaders.ts` (noise, fresnel, soft points), `mulberry32` for deterministic data, Lenis + GSAP ticker as wired.

## Rendering budget
- Particle counts go in `COUNTS` with `high` and `low` tiers; never hard-code counts.
- Animate in shaders via uniforms; update uniforms through material refs in `useFrame`.
- Hide whole groups (`visible = false`) when their fade reaches 0 so they cost no draw calls.
- Prefer one `points`/`lineSegments` per effect over many meshes. Keep large additive glow planes few.
- No post-processing unless it is gated to the `high` tier and measured.
- Respect the existing DPR cap and `PerformanceMonitor`; never raise them.

## React and DOM
- No per-frame React state. Mutate refs, uniforms or DOM directly (see `FeaturePlayer` progress bar).
- Scroll animations: GSAP `scrub` timelines inside `useGSAP` with a `scope`, so they reverse automatically.
- Animate only `transform`, `opacity`, `clip-path`. Avoid animating `filter`, layout or large blurs.
- Sticky (`position: sticky`) over GSAP `pin` for long sections.

## Loading
- Client-only 3D loads through `next/dynamic` with `ssr: false` from a client component.
- No new images or textures unless essential; use `next/image` with explicit size, `.webp`, lazy by default.
- Video: `preload="metadata"`, `playsInline`, no autoplay, pause when scrolled out of view.
- Don't add dependencies for things the current stack already does.

## Reduced motion and cleanup
- Honour `motion.reduced` / `prefers-reduced-motion`: no Lenis, slower ambient motion, no forced camera flights.
- Dispose geometries/materials/textures you create outside JSX; let R3F dispose JSX-created ones.
- Remove event listeners, observers and tickers in effect/`useGSAP` cleanup.

## Before finishing
- `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx eslint app features` pass.
- `npx next build` succeeds; check route JS size did not grow unexpectedly.
- Check DevTools Performance (frame rate while scrolling) and Memory (no growth on repeated scroll up/down).
